Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 10/20/2023]
1.  Strengths of measured resonances are adopted from Endt 1990, and normalized to the Er = 1800 keV resonance (Sargood 1982).
2.  Er = 634 keV: S(p,g) = 1.8 meV listed in Endt 1990 is erroneous. The correct value is S(p,g) = 3.4 meV (Pieter Endt, private communication, 1996). Assumed 30%
    uncertainty in the strength [wg = (1.65+-0.50)e-3 eV] since no uncertainty value is reported in the literature. Proton width is estimated using experimental 
    C2S value. Since Gp >> Gg, the gamma-ray partial width can be obtained from the resonance strength. 
3.  Direct capture S factor estimated using C2S = 0.95, which is the average of Endt 1977, Endt 1990, Guillot et al. 1991.
